  "interpretation": "Both backends completed Bink with exit-0 traces on the same XEX, host, runtime, resources and plugin pair. Xenos reached the scene gate and received Start/A/Start; Native did not reach the gate, so post-gate inputs are not comparable. The first manager+11012 operation mismatch followed five common writes: Native completion sub_823B85D0 decremented 1 to 0 for token 0xC0000000; 245 ms later Xenos producer sub_823B31A0 incremented 1 to 2 for a tag-35 record. The Native physical-alias queue head writer repeatedly moved by -6 while Xenos writes were all +2 in this capture. These are candidate differences for P2 audit, not proof that Xenos is correct or that a particular interrupt caused the Native state.",
